# SitePilot — AI-friendly code

A person (or AI) with no extra context must be able to edit one file safely.

## Layers (this repo, not a Liparta tree)

- `features/<domain>/lib/` — pure logic, no React
- `features/<domain>/components/` — UI only; call lib, do not embed formulas
- `features/<domain>/config.ts` or `lib/*-config.ts` — titles, labels, thresholds, tokens
- `shared/types/` and `features/<domain>/lib/types.ts` — types only
- `app/` — routes and wiring only
- `database/NNN-name.sql` — migrations (user runs them in SQL Editor)
- `tests/` — colocate by domain

Do not invent a top-level `liparta/` or `config/` rewrite. New code follows the layers above. When you touch a messy file, extract **the piece you change**; do not restructure the whole app in one turn.

## File size (new and extracted files)

- One file, one job
- New lib modules: prefer under 150 lines
- New components: prefer under 200 lines
- Functions: prefer under 30 lines
- Existing giants (e.g. manager dashboard): extract only the slice in scope

## Imports

List dependencies explicitly. No `import * from`. Prefer
`import { calculateCpi } from '@/features/evm/lib/metrics'` over barrel stars.

## Allowed imports

- config/types → nothing from UI or app
- lib → config, types, other lib (never components or `app/`)
- components → lib, config, types, other components
- `app/` → features, shared

Forbidden: lib importing components; circular imports.

## New feature order

1. Types
2. Config (labels, thresholds)
3. Lib (pure functions + tests)
4. Components
5. Wire in `app/`
